      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6a6e166e50134251b816ed79|full_name} Your logs indicate yt-dlp is trying to download the pre-muxed 360p video/audio (`-f=18`) from YouTube with the `android_vr` extractor, as intended.\n\nIf `%LocalAppdata%Low\\VRChat\\VRChat\\Tools\\yt-dlp.exe` is version 2026.07.04 (modified by VRChat) - shown in file properties and in `yt-dlp.exe --version` output - there's not much that can be done about this as of writing this right now, because there's no newer stable yt-dlp release yet.\n\nIf you feel adventurous and technically adept, you can debug with:\n\n1. yt-dlp 2026.07.04 (upstream) from: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/tag/2026.07.04\n\n2. yt-dlp nightly 2026.07.09.234832 or later from: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds/releases\n\nand share if the output of:\n\n1. `.\\yt-dlp.exe --version`\n\n2. `.\\yt-dlp.exe --extractor-args \"youtube:player_client=android_vr\" -F https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEAC8eeQWcg`\n\nfrom both versions. You may also replace the`-F` flag with `-f=18` to test downloading it directly and see if there's any change between these versions. It targets this commit from nightly: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/commit/59d9ae606a24a80523da35de9fb75b71eb35b501\n\nI'm unable to replicate your issue here myself with my connection, so you may be part of an A/B test by YouTube.",
